#!/bin/sh
# Generic qrexec RPC service: bridges this call's stdio to
# 127.0.0.1:<port> on whichever qube this is installed on, where
# <port> is the RPC argument from a call shaped like
# "local.ConnectTCP+<port>" (e.g. ai-stack-gpu-tunnel.service's
# `qrexec-client-vm dom0 local.ConnectTCP+8079`, or a devel qube
# calling `qrexec-client-vm git-server local.ConnectTCP+3000`).
#
# Same script regardless of target -- dom0 and regular qubes alike.
# What's actually reachable through it, and by whom, is entirely
# governed by whatever qrexec policy (always dom0-side, per Qubes'
# own architecture) references this service -- see qubes-rpc-user
# (dom0 access) and gitea-tor-forge (git-server access) for the
# policies that currently use this.
#
# RECONSTRUCTED, NOT VERIFIED AGAINST A REAL DOM0 FILE: this package
# was built from a session with no working qrexec connection to any
# real Qubes dom0, so this could not be diffed against whatever's
# actually installed at /etc/qubes-rpc/local.ConnectTCP there. This is
# the standard community implementation of this exact pattern. Diff it
# against a real dom0's file before trusting this package to reproduce
# it, and remove this notice once confirmed identical (or replace the
# body below with the real contents if they differ).

port="${QREXEC_SERVICE_ARGUMENT:-$1}"
exec socat STDIO TCP:127.0.0.1:"${port}"
